WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.417 --> 00:00:07.295
If a vegan falls in the forest ...

00:00:07.295 --> 00:00:09.923
(Laughter)

00:00:09.965 --> 00:00:15.637
And no one's there
to hear them say, "I'm vegan!"

00:00:15.679 --> 00:00:18.014
(Laughter)

00:00:18.723 --> 00:00:20.934
Are they even really vegan?

00:00:20.976 --> 00:00:24.396
(Laughter)

00:00:24.938 --> 00:00:29.192
(Laughter and applause)

00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:35.991
I like to preface conversations
about my dietary habits with jokes

00:00:36.032 --> 00:00:39.744
because brains love the ha-has

00:00:39.786 --> 00:00:43.582
and because sometimes you say
the word "vegan"

00:00:43.582 --> 00:00:47.168
and people get a little afraid.

00:00:48.378 --> 00:00:51.840
Their mind immediately conjures

00:00:51.881 --> 00:00:55.802
this nonexistent super vegan

00:00:55.844 --> 00:01:00.765
who's an amalgam of every annoying thing
they've ever heard a vegan say.

00:01:00.807 --> 00:01:02.225
(Laughter)

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:05.437
And at that point, they're checked out.

00:01:06.146 --> 00:01:09.733
Now if you've managed
to somehow avoid the zeitgeist

00:01:09.774 --> 00:01:12.569
for the last 15 or 20 years,

00:01:12.569 --> 00:01:14.863
one, tell me how.

00:01:14.904 --> 00:01:19.784
(Laughter)

00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:24.122
Two, I will tell you what vegan means,
because I'm sure you're dying to know.

00:01:24.956 --> 00:01:29.836
So vegan is both a diet
completely free of animal products

00:01:29.836 --> 00:01:33.715
and a person who follows that diet,

00:01:33.757 --> 00:01:36.635
often used interchangeably
with "plant-based."

00:01:36.635 --> 00:01:41.514
But plant-based
means "vegan" but not vegan.

00:01:41.514 --> 00:01:43.391
(Laughter)

00:01:43.933 --> 00:01:48.396
Like, not necessarily done to decrease
animal suffering per se,

00:01:48.438 --> 00:01:51.107
but maybe to help one's health.

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:56.237
But that is not the argument
we came to have today.

00:01:56.237 --> 00:01:57.614
No siree, Bob.

00:01:57.656 --> 00:01:59.783
(Laughter)

00:01:59.824 --> 00:02:02.535
I see some sweet-spot
minds looking to tussle.

00:02:02.577 --> 00:02:03.995
Not at my TED Talk.

00:02:04.037 --> 00:02:09.250
(Laughter)

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:13.630
Now I am an outdoor educator,

00:02:13.672 --> 00:02:16.675
I am a wild food forager,

00:02:16.716 --> 00:02:19.844
I am a reluctant social media star.

00:02:19.886 --> 00:02:21.888
(Laughter)

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:24.182
And yes, I am a vegan.

00:02:24.474 --> 00:02:25.642
Audience: Whoo!

00:02:26.101 --> 00:02:27.477
Thank you.

00:02:27.477 --> 00:02:29.688
That's not the reaction I usually get.

00:02:29.729 --> 00:02:30.897
(Laughter)

00:02:31.356 --> 00:02:32.524
At the age of five,

00:02:32.524 --> 00:02:35.527
upon realizing that the cows in the fields

00:02:35.568 --> 00:02:39.197
and the cows on my dad's grill
were the same cows ...

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:41.616
(Laughter)

00:02:41.616 --> 00:02:45.412
I asked my parents
if I could go vegetarian.

00:02:45.453 --> 00:02:47.539
To which they said,

00:02:47.539 --> 00:02:51.292
"Sure, but let's wait
until you're done growing first."

00:02:51.751 --> 00:02:57.215
So sure that I would change my mind
over the next five to nine years.

00:02:58.341 --> 00:02:59.759
Well.

00:03:00.301 --> 00:03:02.429
Shortly after my 12th birthday,

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:05.515
I took the plunge,
and I gave up meat completely.

00:03:06.141 --> 00:03:09.936
It took another 12 years for me
to give up eggs and dairy.

00:03:09.978 --> 00:03:14.816
And now between the veganism
and the foraging,

00:03:14.858 --> 00:03:20.864
I have one of the more
eclectic pantries in the world.

00:03:20.864 --> 00:03:23.700
(Video) Meet the Indigo Milk Cap.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:26.035
Let's make a fancy dessert out of seaweed.

00:03:26.077 --> 00:03:27.829
Here is a mimosa tree.

00:03:27.871 --> 00:03:30.165
Please be a puffball!
Please be a puffball!

00:03:30.206 --> 00:03:31.708
(Laughter)

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.251
It was a puffball.

00:03:34.753 --> 00:03:40.550
Now, foraging is the art/science
of identifying, collecting

00:03:40.592 --> 00:03:43.178
and eating wild food.

00:03:43.553 --> 00:03:49.559
So if anyone's ever convinced you
to try dandelions or wood sorrel,

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:52.604
congratulations, you're a forager too.

00:03:53.855 --> 00:03:58.109
When my mom told me
that there was a bunch of free food

00:03:58.151 --> 00:04:01.279
hanging out in lawns and sidewalks ...

00:04:01.279 --> 00:04:02.864
(Laughter)

00:04:02.864 --> 00:04:05.116
my mind was blown.

00:04:05.617 --> 00:04:11.498
All these free fruits, veggies and fungi
that didn't require your water,

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:13.666
didn’t require your time

00:04:13.708 --> 00:04:15.668
and often were healthier

00:04:15.668 --> 00:04:18.505
than their counterparts
in the grocery store.

00:04:18.546 --> 00:04:21.090
Cute little fun fact just between us,

00:04:21.132 --> 00:04:23.468
we did this thing over the last 100 years

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:28.681
where we bred foods to travel easier,
be bigger, taste milder.

00:04:28.973 --> 00:04:33.603
And that often breeds out the nutrition.

00:04:34.813 --> 00:04:39.317
Let's take, for example,
Purslane or Verdolagas,

00:04:39.359 --> 00:04:42.278
if you are in a Spanish-speaking
part of the Americas.

00:04:42.779 --> 00:04:47.909
It is a weed that grows out
of sidewalk cracks in the summertime.

00:04:49.118 --> 00:04:52.997
It is chock-full of Omega-3s,
and it ain’t a fish.

00:04:53.915 --> 00:04:56.376
Iron, get out of here, Popeye.

00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:57.418
(Laughter)

00:04:57.418 --> 00:04:58.711
And vitamin C,

00:04:58.753 --> 00:05:01.005
your immune system will thank you.

00:05:01.881 --> 00:05:05.051
Sometimes I will just stand
in my neighborhood,

00:05:05.093 --> 00:05:06.886
looking at the ground like.

00:05:07.887 --> 00:05:11.224
(Laughter)

00:05:11.266 --> 00:05:15.436
And I'm baffled that no one
else seems to care.

00:05:17.272 --> 00:05:23.486
Now I am a forager and a vegan
for much the same reason.

00:05:23.486 --> 00:05:27.115
My love of this planet
and its inhabitants.

00:05:27.907 --> 00:05:30.076
But let me tell you,

00:05:30.118 --> 00:05:32.120
between those two identifiers,

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:35.748
it's pretty hard to get people
to try my food.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:38.543
(Laughter)

00:05:38.585 --> 00:05:43.673
You tell someone something's vegan
and you're already met with skepticism.

00:05:43.715 --> 00:05:47.302
Tell them it’s vegan and you pulled
half of it out of the ground ...

00:05:47.343 --> 00:05:49.512
(Laughter)

00:05:49.512 --> 00:05:51.055
It's a tough sell.

00:05:52.473 --> 00:05:57.270
So today I'm going to give
all of you my tips, my tricks

00:05:57.312 --> 00:06:00.189
on getting people to expand their palette

00:06:00.189 --> 00:06:02.942
and try wild vegan foods consensually.

00:06:03.276 --> 00:06:05.653
(Laughter)

00:06:05.695 --> 00:06:08.615
This is not the Lying Liar show.

00:06:09.032 --> 00:06:12.952
It is the Slightly Annoying
but Ultimately Lovable Tall Vegan show.

00:06:12.994 --> 00:06:15.288
(Laughter)

00:06:15.288 --> 00:06:20.668
So today we are going to be making
a snack that happens to be vegan,

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.670
happens to be great for the planet,

00:06:22.712 --> 00:06:25.381
happens to use one
of my favorite ingredients.

00:06:25.381 --> 00:06:28.509
We are making sweet and salty kelp chips,

00:06:28.509 --> 00:06:31.638
a Korean snack known as Dasima Twigak.

00:06:32.889 --> 00:06:34.390
Oh, thank you.

00:06:34.432 --> 00:06:37.018
A "woo" for the pronunciation,
I was worried about it.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:40.229
(Laughter)

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:42.649
Now I know all
of y'all's kids are obsessed

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.485
with those nori seaweed snacks,

00:06:45.485 --> 00:06:47.528
so why not kick it up a notch --

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:48.947
Sorry --

00:06:48.988 --> 00:06:53.868
(Laughter)

00:06:53.910 --> 00:06:57.789
With a locally foraged
ingredient: bull kelp.

00:06:58.164 --> 00:07:00.583
I foraged this right here in Vancouver.

00:07:01.042 --> 00:07:05.129
(Applause and cheers)

00:07:06.172 --> 00:07:10.802
Now I'm going to go
and start chipifying this seaweed.

00:07:11.552 --> 00:07:13.763
Very official kitchen shears.

00:07:14.597 --> 00:07:16.808
And while I'm doing that,

00:07:16.849 --> 00:07:20.520
I'm going to give you my first tip.

00:07:21.187 --> 00:07:24.732
When introducing a dish
to skeptical mouths,

00:07:24.732 --> 00:07:29.946
it is best to use a dish that is not
pretending to be something else.

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.448
(Applause)

00:07:32.448 --> 00:07:34.117
You know.

00:07:34.993 --> 00:07:38.329
That way, they have no prior associations,

00:07:38.329 --> 00:07:43.251
no memories to be comparing it to
of their mother's version of it.

00:07:43.292 --> 00:07:45.253
(Laughter)

00:07:45.253 --> 00:07:48.715
Maybe they have no opinions
about it at all.

00:07:48.756 --> 00:07:51.759
I'm going to spritz these
with a little sunflower oil.

00:07:52.385 --> 00:07:53.511
Ooh.

00:07:54.137 --> 00:07:55.304
Smokey.

00:07:57.765 --> 00:08:02.020
Now, seaweed and sea vegetables in general

00:08:02.061 --> 00:08:05.606
are a very exciting food space.

00:08:06.399 --> 00:08:09.861
They don't require fresh water.

00:08:10.236 --> 00:08:11.696
They don't require fertilizer.

00:08:11.696 --> 00:08:13.823
They don't even require land.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:18.036
They're just hanging out
in the salty seas, creating ecosystems,

00:08:18.077 --> 00:08:20.413
creating oxygen for all of us to breathe,

00:08:20.413 --> 00:08:23.791
and creating these amino acid-rich snacks.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:27.795
In this day and age,
seaweed is truly future-minded food.

00:08:28.212 --> 00:08:30.882
They're an option I wish
more people would reach for,

00:08:30.923 --> 00:08:36.971
as runoff, water access, labor issues
and monoculturing

00:08:36.971 --> 00:08:40.850
plague a lot of modern agriculture
here in North America.

00:08:41.851 --> 00:08:43.019
Yeah.

00:08:43.061 --> 00:08:45.480
(Applause)

00:08:45.521 --> 00:08:48.733
Also they taste real good.

00:08:49.442 --> 00:08:54.614
Those amino acids do a lot more
than adding umami to your dishes.

00:08:54.655 --> 00:09:00.578
Bull help on average packs
15.3 percent protein by weight.

00:09:00.912 --> 00:09:05.917
That is for everyone who asks
where vegans get their protein from.

00:09:06.417 --> 00:09:07.919
We're fine.

00:09:07.919 --> 00:09:10.505
(Laughter)

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:15.426
Now as I said before,
this dish is nothing new.

00:09:15.468 --> 00:09:18.679
It's a popular bar snack
in parts of Korea,

00:09:18.721 --> 00:09:25.228
and we actually have a lot of accidentally
vegan recipes historically.

00:09:25.228 --> 00:09:27.772
And the reason for that
is because up until recently,

00:09:27.772 --> 00:09:29.816
we did not eat this much meat.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:34.237
Which is going to lead to my second tip.

00:09:34.237 --> 00:09:36.405
It's a little spicy, a little touchy.

00:09:36.405 --> 00:09:40.243
Hopefully the promise of a food reveal
will get you all through it.

00:09:42.036 --> 00:09:43.412
And it is this.

00:09:44.789 --> 00:09:49.877
Explain to your friends that the way
that we are eating is not sustainable.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:51.838
Yeah.

00:09:51.838 --> 00:09:53.172
(Applause)

00:09:53.172 --> 00:09:54.340
It's not.

00:09:54.382 --> 00:09:55.591
(Applause)

00:09:55.633 --> 00:10:00.263
As we are constantly reaching
for more land and more fresh water,

00:10:00.304 --> 00:10:05.810
we have set a precedent
that our planet can not keep up with.

00:10:07.228 --> 00:10:10.439
Tell them you are not trying
to change their entire life.

00:10:10.857 --> 00:10:13.276
You just want them to be
a bit more thoughtful

00:10:13.317 --> 00:10:14.652
with some of their choices,

00:10:14.652 --> 00:10:16.154
to go for those kelp chips

00:10:16.195 --> 00:10:19.657
instead of maybe pork rinds
from the convenience store.

00:10:20.283 --> 00:10:24.579
I find that introducing people
to wild foods in their area

00:10:24.579 --> 00:10:28.749
is an excellent way to foster
their connection to their food.

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:32.962
And it's a way that fosters
that connection over shame.

00:10:33.546 --> 00:10:37.925
And it shares a snack
instead of an infographic

00:10:37.925 --> 00:10:40.845
or a shocking piece of media.

00:10:42.013 --> 00:10:44.515
Now moment of truth time.

00:10:44.557 --> 00:10:46.851
Let's see how these guys
are doing in here.

00:10:48.102 --> 00:10:50.438
Oh, yes, this will do nicely.

00:10:53.149 --> 00:10:56.736
Now I'm going to be real real
with all of you

00:10:56.777 --> 00:10:59.572
because I would never
not be real real with you.

00:11:00.656 --> 00:11:02.491
Some people ...

00:11:02.533 --> 00:11:04.744
OK, get out of there, babies.

00:11:07.330 --> 00:11:10.041
(Laughter)

00:11:10.458 --> 00:11:14.086
Some people are going to be salty.

00:11:14.086 --> 00:11:17.089
And that's a funny thing for me
to say, because this is salt.

00:11:17.089 --> 00:11:19.717
(Laughter)

00:11:20.051 --> 00:11:22.428
And that's just the way it goes,

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.057
we don't get to choose the pace
at which people change,

00:11:26.057 --> 00:11:28.684
if they choose to change at all.

00:11:30.353 --> 00:11:34.565
But, some people -- this is sugar --

00:11:35.942 --> 00:11:37.276
will be sweet.

00:11:38.986 --> 00:11:42.698
They will appreciate you
for meeting them where they are.

00:11:43.449 --> 00:11:46.202
For sharing a snack and a smile,

00:11:46.244 --> 00:11:50.206
and maybe you extending
that bit of compassion to them

00:11:50.206 --> 00:11:55.253
will make them make some big changes
moving forward in their life.

00:11:56.712 --> 00:11:57.922
And who knows,

00:11:57.922 --> 00:12:01.592
maybe next time they'll be gutsy enough
to try acorn cheese or something.

00:12:03.844 --> 00:12:05.638
So share that snack.

00:12:06.389 --> 00:12:08.057
And make that memory.

00:12:08.808 --> 00:12:12.853
Thank you all so much
for coming to my talk.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.273
Ooh.

00:12:15.314 --> 00:12:16.774
That was a nice crunch.

00:12:16.774 --> 00:12:18.234
Happy snacking.

00:12:18.276 --> 00:12:19.527
Don't die.

00:12:19.527 --> 00:12:25.449
(Cheers and applause)

